IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-21: Article 21 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): cooperation with competent authorities.
-- Lines 430-434 of the consolidated text. Unchanged by the Omnibus. Article 2(13) names Article 21 among the obligations whose application may be limited for an Article 6(1) system (the gate).
-- Paragraphs 1 and 2 are duties "upon a reasoned request": with no such request the paragraph does not speak (NOTHING-kind, limited by its own wording; fork F-when-upon in NOTES.md).
-- Paragraph 3 addresses the competent authority (an official, so no seat): it is encoded for what it means to the provider, that what it supplies is treated in confidence.

DECLARE `Art 21 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 21(1) provide the competent authority all the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 21(2) give the requesting competent authority access to the automatically generated logs`

DECLARE `Art 21(3) body` IS ONE OF
    `Art 21(3) competent authority`

DECLARE `Art 21(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 21(3) treat the information obtained in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78`

§ `Article 21(1): information and documentation upon a reasoned request`

-- src:432 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems shall, upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, provide that authority all the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2, in a language which can be easily understood by the authority in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union as indicated by the Member State concerned.
@ref Art 21(1) (src:432)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has provided that authority all the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and documentation is in a language which can be easily understood by the authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that language is one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union as indicated by the Member State concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(1) the provider has provided the competent authority the information and documentation upon a reasoned request` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall, upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, provide that authority all the information and documentation" (no reasoned request has been made)
        ELSE
             IF `the provider has provided that authority all the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2` AND `the information and documentation is in a language which can be easily understood by the authority` AND `that language is one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union as indicated by the Member State concerned`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, provide that authority all the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2, in a language which can be easily understood by the authority in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union as indicated by the Member State concerned"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 21, "", 0)

@ref Art 21(1) (src:432)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 21 act`
`Art 21(1) the provider's duty to provide the competent authority the information and documentation upon a reasoned request` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 21(1) provide the competent authority all the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate conformity were not provided"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or no reasoned request has been made
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 21, "", 0)


§ `Article 21(2): access to the automatically generated logs upon a reasoned request, to the extent under the provider's control`

-- src:433 | 2. Upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, providers shall also give the requesting competent authority, as applicable, access to the automatically generated logs of the high-risk AI system referred to in Article 12(1), to the extent such logs are under their control.
@ref Art 21(2) (src:433)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system referred to in Article 12(1) are under the provider's control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has given the requesting competent authority access to the logs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(2) the provider has given the requesting competent authority access to the automatically generated logs` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, providers shall also give the requesting competent authority ... access to the automatically generated logs" (no reasoned request has been made)
        ELSE
             IF NOT `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system referred to in Article 12(1) are under the provider's control`
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the extent such logs are under their control" (the logs are not under the provider's control)
             ELSE
                  IF `the provider has given the requesting competent authority access to the logs`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, providers shall also give the requesting competent authority, as applicable, access to the automatically generated logs of the high-risk AI system referred to in Article 12(1), to the extent such logs are under their control"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 21, "", 0)

@ref Art 21(2) (src:433)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system referred to in Article 12(1) are under the provider's control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 21 act`
`Art 21(2) the provider's duty to give the requesting competent authority access to the automatically generated logs` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `a competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider` AND `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system referred to in Article 12(1) are under the provider's control`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 21(2) give the requesting competent authority access to the automatically generated logs`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the requesting competent authority was not given access to the automatically generated logs"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, no reasoned request has been made, or the logs are not under the provider's control
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 21, "", 0)


§ `Article 21(3): information obtained by a competent authority is treated in accordance with Article 78 (addressed to the authority; encoded for what it means to the provider)`

-- JUST TRUE: the information was obtained pursuant to this Article, so it "shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78";
-- NOTHING: the paragraph does not speak of information obtained otherwise (silent). Article 78 itself is P4's.
-- src:434 | 3. Any information obtained by a competent authority pursuant to this Article shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78.
@ref Art 21(3) (src:434)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the information was obtained by a competent authority pursuant to Article 21` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 21(3) the information obtained by a competent authority is to be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the information was obtained by a competent authority pursuant to Article 21`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 3 speaks of information obtained pursuant to this Article only
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 21, "", 0)

-- src:434 | 3. Any information obtained by a competent authority pursuant to this Article shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78.
@ref Art 21(3) (src:434)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the information was obtained by a competent authority pursuant to Article 21` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Art 21(3) body` `Art 21(3) act`
`Art 21(3) the competent authority's duty to treat the information obtained in accordance with Article 78` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the information was obtained by a competent authority pursuant to Article 21`
    THEN PARTY `Art 21(3) competent authority`
         MUST `Art 21(3) treat the information obtained in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Art 21(3) competent authority` BECAUSE "the information obtained pursuant to Article 21 was not treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the information was not obtained pursuant to this Article
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 21, "", 0)
